<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mujir al-Din Abaq</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 1140–1154</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mujir al-Din Abaq was the last Burid ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a>, reigning from 1140 to 1154, largely under the control of powerful ministers. Damascus kept a cautious alliance with the crusader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-jerusalem">Kingdom of Jerusalem</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zengid-dynasty">Zengids</a>, yet was besieged by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-crusade">Second Crusade</a> in 1148. Losing the support of the townspeople, he surrendered the city to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nur-al-din">Nur al-Din</a> in 1154, uniting Muslim <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>.</p></div>
